<h2>Course notes</h2>
<p>Every module in the outline above links to its full lecture notes. Each follows one chapter of Bishop &amp; Bishop's
  <em>Deep Learning: Foundations and Concepts</em>, the course text, and explains the same ideas in its own words: the
  model and why it works, the derivations that matter, code with its real output, checks of that code against
  closed forms, finite differences, or PyTorch's own layers, figures, and exercises. Where a chapter revisits material
  developed at length in the <a href="{{ '/teaching/introml/' | relative_url }}">Introduction to Machine Learning</a>
  notes, the module is shorter and links there. The book remains the reference, with the full derivations and many
  more exercises.</p>
